{
  "id": 505942985,
  "iid": 25738,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "ZIP File: Add ZIP file support to Fileshark",
  "description": "In a possible case of Zawinski's Law, support examining ZIP files\n(and other files that are ZIP files, like JAR, ODS, DOCX, etc.)\nand extract contents with Export Objects.\n\nThis uses the (safer) \"streaming\" reading technique like Mark\nAdler's sunzip[1] rather than scanning from the end for the\nCentral Directory Listing, which might not be possible when this\nis called by the media type dissector. Also no recursive dissection\nof the files contained within the ZIP archive, for another ZIP\nbomb mitigation.\n\nZIP is already used by AppleTalk's Zone Information Protocol\n(packet-atalk is still seeing recent commits, with some in the\npast two weeks, despite the use of the past tense on AppleTalk's\nWikipedia page), so use \"zipfile\" for the unique filter name\nand \"ZIP_FILE\" (by analogy with \"MIME_FILE\") for the unique\nshort name.\n\n[1] - https://github.com/madler/sunzip",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2026-07-10T14:09:04.874Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-07-11T12:37:31.317Z",
